# {{PROJECT_TITLE}} — project rules (always on)

This folder is a **Project**: one investigation into {{PHYSICAL_SYSTEM}}, hosting many **campaigns** (versioned
attempts) and **sessions** (ad-hoc work). These rules bind every agent working anywhere under this tree.
`PROJECT.md` is the overview — the mission, everything known about the system, the durable decisions, and
§Lineage, the index of what has been done; `README.md` is the short directory map. (Each campaign also has its
own `CLAUDE.md` with the loop spine; this file adds the project-level rules on top.)

## Structure
`Project → Campaign → Experiment` (+ ad-hoc `sessions/`). Campaigns live in `campaigns/<name>/`; ad-hoc work in
`sessions/<YYYY-MM-DD>_<slug>/`; the canonical data in `data/`; promoted shared artifacts in purpose-named
project-level dirs (`scripts/`, `models/`, …, created on demand); one `reports/`.

## Non-negotiable rules
1. **Shared data and docs are referenced, never copied.** Use `../../data`, `../../PROJECT.md`, and the
   promoted project-level dirs (`../../scripts`, `../../models`, …) by relative path. **Never copy the data
   or any part of the overview into a campaign, never write into `data/`.** Copies are what break paths and
   fork the record — don't create them.
2. **Everything is indexed in `PROJECT.md` §Lineage.** A campaign gets a row; a session gets a row; a
   within-campaign version bump and an artifact promotion each get a one-line change-record. Nothing
   significant happens off the ledger.
3. **Campaign vs session.** One optimizable **frozen metric driving a loop** → a **campaign** (`new-campaign`).
   Exploration / debugging / a one-off analysis with no frozen metric → a **session** (a `sessions/<…>/` folder
   with a `NOTES.md`). When unsure, start a session; promote later.
4. **Findings at their true tier.** A session finding, or an unverified result, is recorded as such — it does
   **not** enter `PROJECT.md` §Updates from discoveries unless it passed `verify`, and every entry there cites
   the source campaign's verdict artifact by path. The full evidence stays in the campaign that produced it
   (`results/JOURNAL.md` §Findings + `results/verdicts/`); the project holds the synthesis and the pointer,
   never a copy trusted on its own.
5. **Invalidating updates fork-and-archive — they do not silently carry forward.** If a change (e.g. a fixed
   forward-model bug, a corrected dataset) **invalidates or makes misleading** a campaign's prior findings,
   **fork a fresh-ledger campaign and archive the old one** (`campaigns/_archive/`, frozen, still in §Lineage).
   The old `results/`/`JOURNAL` do NOT become the new effort's working documents; carry forward only findings
   that survive **re-verification**, with provenance. A journal built on a known-bad model must never steer the
   next effort silently.
6. **Consumed artifacts come from the promoted project-level dirs.** If a sibling campaign froze something you
   depend on (a forward model, a training set), reference the **promoted, versioned** copy at the project level
   (`../../models/<artifact>_<ver>`, …) — never the sibling's working folder. A promoted artifact has a
   `PROJECT.md` §Lineage promotion line; an artifact without one is a working file, not a dependency. Declare
   the FROZEN/MUTABLE relationship in your campaign's `campaign.md`.
7. **`PROJECT.md` is edited by tier.** OPEN sections (the system/instrument/equations depth, gotchas,
   references, appends to §Updates from discoveries and §Lineage): edit when new information arrives, citing
   the evidence. GUARDED sections (§Mission, §Standing constraints, closed §Durable decisions entries):
   append/supersede, never rewrite; every change carries a §Durable decisions entry; a change that alters what
   a **running** campaign is held to needs the user. §Standing constraints is delivered into every spawned
   prompt of every campaign — treat editing it like editing a frozen gate.

## Portability
All internal references are relative; the whole `<project>/` tree relocates as one unit. The only absolute path
is the resolved `data_path` (in `PROJECT.md` §Mission) when the canonical data lives off-tree.
